# ── Line endings ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This is a Windows-primary checkout with `core.autocrlf=true`, so the working
# tree is CRLF while the index is LF. That worked by accident, not by contract:
# nothing here said so, an agent or an editor on another platform could commit
# CRLF blobs, and a multi-line patch written against `\n` silently matches
# nothing (it has cost this repo two no-op'd patches). `* text=auto` makes the
# LF-in-the-index rule the repository's, independent of anyone's git config.
* text=auto

# Files that are EXECUTED or PARSED by tools that are LF-only or LF-happier —
# pinned rather than left to `text=auto`'s heuristic, so a checkout with
# `core.autocrlf=true` still gets LF on disk for these.
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.cjs   text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf

# Git hooks run under sh — they must stay LF even on Windows checkouts.
.githooks/* text eol=lf

# Lockfiles and generated bundles: never diffed by hand, always LF.
package-lock.json text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never touched by EOL conversion, never diffed as text.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp3   binary
*.wav   binary
*.sqlite binary
